# Line endings (issue #4085): without this file, Windows checkouts with
# core.autocrlf=true get CRLF working-tree files. That breaks Jekyll's default
# excerpt separator ("\n\n" never matches "\r\n\r\n", so a local excerpt becomes
# the whole post) and bash scripts such as infrastructure/bootstrap/deploy.sh
# under WSL. Text is LF in the index AND the working tree on every platform.
# No file here needs CRLF (no .bat/.cmd/.ps1 are tracked).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary types: never normalize. (text=auto already detects these; the explicit
# list guards against a byte sequence that merely looks like text.)
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.webm binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
